Patch — sglang/gravityocr_selfspec.patch
  Copyright 2026 Trillion Labs. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  A diff against the base commit above. It modifies 25 upstream source files
  under python/sglang/srt/ and python/pyproject.toml, where it relaxes the
  torchao and torchcodec pins (sglang/overrides.txt records the versions used).
  The changes register the SELFSPEC_DIFFUSION speculative-decoding algorithm
  (block-diffusion draft, autoregressive verify) for GLM-OCR checkpoints, add
  the scheduler, cache and CUDA-graph support it needs, and add optional runtime
  optimizations. The modified files keep their upstream copyright headers.
  Pure code; no model weights.
  Differs from the patch in the GravityOCR release in one hunk only:
  entrypoints/http_server.py, where /server_info no longer returns the API and
  admin keys (added in this repository; to be upstreamed to GravityOCR).
